      "id": "blood_oxygen_transport",
      "title": "Red blood cells and blood volume",
      "area": "Hematology",
      "relationship": "Hemoglobin is the oxygen-carrying protein in red blood cells, and hematocrit is the share of blood made up of red cells. Both are concentrations, so they depend on red-cell mass and on plasma volume. Ferritin reflects iron stores but also rises with inflammation.",
      "spaceflightContext": "Spaceflight reduces plasma volume and red-cell mass (often called space anaemia), so concentration values are interpreted together with volume measurements.",
      "handbookIds": ["cv-014", "cv-015", "cv-075", "cv-076"],
      "members": [
        { "id": "cv-075", "name": "Hemoglobin", "role": "red_cells" },
