    {
      "id": "bone_mineral",
      "title": "Bone and mineral health",
      "area": "Bone and mineral health",
      "relationship": "Bone is constantly broken down (resorption) and rebuilt (formation). Resorption markers such as CTX, pyridinoline and deoxypyridinoline reflect breakdown; formation markers such as P1NP and osteocalcin reflect rebuilding, and the two are interpreted together. Calcium, phosphate, parathyroid hormone (PTH) and vitamin D regulate the mineral supply to bone, and bone-density scans show the structural result over months.",
      "spaceflightContext": "Without the loading of gravity, bone breakdown increases in microgravity; resistance exercise, calcium and vitamin D are the main countermeasures.",
      "handbookIds": ["bone-001", "bone-009", "bone-013", "bone-016", "bone-018", "bone-019", "bone-043"],
